From: mklab <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH 40/40] nothing published the memory map: /memory carried only its name

/memory has always been a node with a `name` and nothing else on both x86 arches,
on every path -- multiboot and coreboot alike. On ppc and sparc the `reg` is a
by-product of ofmem, which those arches lean on (20 references in arch/ppc, 6 in
arch/sparc32); arch/x86 says in its own openbios.c that it has none, and
arch/amd64 mentions ofmem nowhere. So no one ever wrote the map into the tree.

Measured on arch/x86 BEFORE writing any of this, because "the coreboot path is
missing it" and "nobody publishes it at all" are different bugs and only the
second was true. x86 multiboot had no reg either.

publish_memory_ranges() lives in libopenbios/init.c so both arches call one
implementation, from arch_init() AFTER openbios_init() -- the device tree does not
exist at the top of arch_init, where find_dev() faults rather than returning 0.

THE CELL COUNTS ARE READ FROM THE ROOT, NOT ASSUMED. A reg is meaningless without
the #address-cells/#size-cells that decode it, and this tree's root declares
`#address-cells 1` and NO #size-cells -- so a hardcoded 2/2 would have produced a
property every consumer misreads. Absent counts fall back to the 1275 defaults.

A RANGE THAT DOES NOT FIT IS DROPPED AND SAID OUT LOUD, never truncated. With one
address cell an address is 32 bits, and this lab routinely puts an NVDIMM at
0x100000000; silently writing the low half would be a property that looks valid
and points somewhere else. Cells are big-endian, high cell first, per 1275 -- the
same trap drivers/pci.c documents after its builders handed set_property() raw
host-order arrays.

Result, with -m 512:

  x86/amd64 multiboot (QEMU e820):     00000000 0009fc00 / 00100000 1fee0000  (511 MB)
  amd64 coreboot (the coreboot table): 00001000 0009f000 / 00100000 1fd71000  (510 MB)

Control: the call was removed from arch/x86 and the smoke track failed with
"/memory carries no 'reg' property".

Arch-tested: x86 amd64 ppc

diff --git a/include/libopenbios/sys_info.h b/include/libopenbios/sys_info.h
--- a/include/libopenbios/sys_info.h
+++ b/include/libopenbios/sys_info.h
@@ -3,6 +3,10 @@
 
 /* Information collected from firmware/bootloader */
 
+/* Publishes the map below into /memory's `reg`; see libopenbios/init.c. */
+struct sys_info;
+extern void publish_memory_ranges(struct sys_info *info);
+
 struct sys_info {
     /* Values passed by bootloader */
     unsigned long boot_type;
